    "result_text": "The build passes with the test green. Let me verify the full logical flow once more by checking the pipeline ordering hasn't been disturbed and that all functions still get their required params (the OfficeFloor start-up would fail at test time otherwise \u2014 and it didn't).\n\nThe implementation is complete. Here's a summary of the change:\n\n## What changed\n\n**`householdId` is now deterministic** \u2014 the first 12 hex characters of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode`, computed for **every** owner (not just declared sharers). Owners with the same last name and postcode now share it automatically.\n\n- **`OwnerIdentities.householdId(Owner)`** (new) \u2014 centralizes the hash; refactored the shared SHA helper so `customerCode` keeps its upper-case 8-char form while `householdId` uses the lower-case 12-char form. Normalized last name = trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, lower-cased.\n\n- **`AssignHousehold`** \u2014 rewritten from a repository-scanning back-filler into a one-liner that stamps `OwnerIdentities.householdId(owner)` on the new owner. Runs before the checks that key off the household.\n\n- **`CheckUniqueIdentity`** \u2014 repurposed into the **household-duplicate block**: rejects (409 `DuplicateIdentityException`) when an existing owner shares the new owner's `householdId`, i.e. same last name + postcode. `sharesHousehold=true` now **only bypasses this block** (declaring an intentional member) rather than creating the link \u2014 the link is implicit in the shared id.\n\n- **`CheckPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 a declared household member (`sharesHousehold=true`) is no longer flagged; `possibleDuplicate` is forced `false`. A declared member is not a suspected duplicate.\n\n- **`HouseholdMembers`** (unchanged) \u2014 already keys the household-size count off `householdId`, so it now naturally counts owners sharing last name + postcode.\n\n- **`DuplicateIdentityException`** and **`openapi.yml`** (`sharesHousehold`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`) \u2014 docs updated to describe the household-keyed behaviour.\n\nThe pipeline order (`build \u2192 household-assign \u2192 identity \u2192 possibleDuplicate \u2192 \u2026`) already had `householdId` fixed before every consumer, so no YAML wiring change was needed.\n\n**Test result:** `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS. The new `coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` acceptance test passes: same last name + postcode yields the same `householdId` (owner `b` bypassing the block via `sharesHousehold`), and a different last name yields a different one.",
